# Workspace quota status owner handoff

These are review artifacts, not installed product changes. The local scheduling
source and tests remain unqualified until the Linux target gate runs.

- iam-composition.review.patch adds only the scheduling dispatch import and
  the authenticated read branch before general Workspace dispatch. It reuses
  h.Workspaces.Service; there is no new cookie, authentication or pool.
  It has not been applied or compiled against the identity owner.
- openapi.review.json describes the module payload and both versioned routes,
  including the existing data envelope, cookie entrances, decimal quantities
  and storage outcome statuses. DEV owns publishing it under api/openapi and
  regenerating the Web client in the same composed feature.
- source-head identifies the current branch parent. New scheduling source is
  still in this lane's worktree; this packet is not a replacement for its
  eventual authored implementation commit.

ARC must admit the quota and reservation tables and exact fresh/restored
catalogs before activating this reader. Production readiness, IAM route tests,
Web translation and UI tests remain open. The module never treats quota status
as a current selected-job explanation or physical placement authority.
